{
  "$comment": "#NEW-133: THE PHRASE GRAMMAR of the issue search: translate(phrase, members, now) -> the structured query string the engine runs (issue-search.json: is:, status:, by:, created:, updated:), or null when the phrase is not a sentence. Deterministic, German + English, no model; web `translateIssueSearchPhrase` (apps/web/src/lib/issue-search-phrase.ts) is the reference and owns the WORD LISTS, mirrored byte for byte on iOS, Android and desktop; every case replays on all four. CASES: {name, now (ISO, UTC), members [{name, email}], phrase, expected (string | null)}. TOKENS: the phrase lowercased, split on whitespace, each token stripped of leading and trailing . , ; : ! ? \" ' ( ); empty tokens go. A token starting with by: is: status: created: updated: or similar: means the text already is a query: null. WALK left to right, first rule wins at each position: (1) DATE: a date phrase, optionally behind up to two lead-in words (aus, seit, since, from, in, im, during, within, während, innerhalb, von, vom, der, dem, den, des, the; consumed only when a date follows). Date phrases: heute|today -> today; gestern|yesterday -> yesterday; LAST unit -> 1d, 7d (week), 1m, 1y; LAST n unit (n = 1..9999) -> <n>d|w|m|y; THIS day -> today; THIS week -> >=<the UTC Monday of now's week>; THIS month -> YYYY-MM of now; THIS year -> >=YYYY-01-01; seit|since|ab|after|nach|from <ISO> -> >=<ISO>; vor|before|bis|until <ISO> -> <<ISO>; a bare valid ISO day or month -> itself; a month name (German or English, full) counts only after a month lead-in (in, im, from, since, seit, aus, during, während) or before a 4-digit year: with the year -> YYYY-MM, without -> the latest such month not after now's month (a month still ahead = last year's). (2) STATUS: `in progress|in arbeit|in bearbeitung` -> status:progress, `in review|im review` -> status:review, then one word: the open words -> is:open, the closed words -> is:closed, backlog, the done words -> status:done, the cancelled words -> status:cancelled, the duplicate words -> status:duplicate. (3) CREATOR: von|vom|by|from followed by a word that is a name word or the email local part of a member -> by:<word>; every following word that is a name word (or the local part) of one of the SAME members joins as another by:. No member: von|vom|by is dropped and the name stays a plain word; from falls through to (4). (4) an updated verb (updated, changed, geändert, aktualisiert, bearbeitet, ...) moves EVERY date to updated: and goes; a noun (issue(s), ticket(s), aufgabe(n), task(s), vorgang) goes and marks the sentence; filler words go; anything else is a word, kept in order. RESULT: null unless a date or a member matched, or a state/status word matched AND a noun was seen (`open issues` is a sentence, `open file dialog` is not). Else the query: is: tokens, status: tokens, by: tokens, the dates (created: or updated:), then the words, each list in first-seen order without repeats, joined by one space; null when that equals the tokens joined (nothing changed). SURFACE (search-list.json): a recognised sentence puts ONE action row `Search: <query>` on top of the search list; picking it replaces the field's text with the query.",
